  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Ranch You're Walking Home Across",
    "overview": "\n**Creative North Star: \"The Ranch You're Walking Home Across\"**\n\nThe dashboard is a place, not a card grid. A layered flat-vector scene (sky, hazed hills, barn, silo, fence, trees, flowers, a dirt trail with a signpost per debt) fills the top of the main area, and the trail from the barn to the debt-free flag is the real progress. Each of the nine themes is a time of day or a season on the same ranch. Everything below the scene sits on the scene's own ground color, so the page reads as the meadow in front of the picture.\n\nSurfaces are soft, large-radius pages lifted by one diffuse tinted shadow. Headings are wooden plank tabs. Ink is a deep tint of the theme hue, never neutral black or gray. Type pairs a fat display face for the headline moment with a rounded friendly UI face; figures are tabular so money never jitters. The mood is warm, confident and playful without being babyish or bank-like. The animals (Debtsy and one friend per theme) stay as characters in the scene and in empty states.\n\nInterior pages other than the dashboard get a short strip (132px phone, 150px tablet, 172px desktop) that carries a cropped piece of the same scene, a plank title and one action, then ordinary ranch cards below it.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "The scene is the hero; modules follow on `--ranch-ground`.",
      "One surface recipe: page-colored card, 24px radius, one soft tinted shadow, no borders.",
      "Plank-tab headings with two nail dots on every module.",
      "Ink and button colors are deep tints of the active theme; dark mode is derived, not separate.",
      "Money is Quicksand 700 tabular; figures roll when they change.",
      "Everything reads CSS custom properties, so a theme change or dark toggle needs no per-theme rules."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Tinted Ink Rule",
        "body": "Text is never gray or black. It is the theme's deep ink or soft ink, so every theme and its night version keeps its hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Alarm Rule",
        "body": "Berry Focus is the single urgent color. It marks the focus debt, the next milestone and errors, and nothing decorative.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token Rule",
        "body": "Components read `--ranch-*` only. A hex value in component CSS is a defect unless it is scene art.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Jobs Rule",
        "body": "Bagel Fat One is for the headline moment and wordmark only. Fredoka names things, Nunito explains, Quicksand counts.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rolling Figure Rule",
        "body": "Money in the sky and today cards uses the RollingNumber digit-wheel; under reduced motion it shows the end state.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Soft Lift Rule",
        "body": "One shadow recipe per surface class, always tinted by `--ranch-sh`. Never a black drop shadow, never a hard offset.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** read surface, ink and state colors from `--ranch-*` tokens so all nine themes and dark mode work.",
      "**Do** open every module and dialog with a plank heading.",
      "**Do** keep money in Quicksand 700 tabular and wrap it in `.num`.",
      "**Do** put the hero action (\"Log a payment\") in the sky and make it a pill in the button color.",
      "**Do** use Berry Focus only for the thing to act on now.",
      "**Do** keep touch targets at 44px or more and give every animation a reduced-motion end state.",
      "**Do** add new Tailwind-era markup to the shell's utility mapping only as a bridge; give the page proper ranch classes when you touch it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** lead a page with a big balance number over a grid of identical cards; the scene and trail come first.",
      "**Don't** use gray text, black text or pure neutral backgrounds inside the shell.",
      "**Don't** use hard offset shadows, card borders or nested cards.",
      "**Don't** make it babyish, bank-like or plain; no gradient-pink pastel wash, no corporate blue dashboard.",
      "**Don't** set Bagel Fat One below headline scale or in running UI text.",
      "**Don't** reuse Berry Focus or the plank brown for decoration.",
      "**Don't** touch the landing page's older look from here, and don't copy its patterns into the app interior."
    ]
  }
